  "definition": {
   "definition": "In the SCB fortnightly statement, 'Investments' is the outstanding total investment by scheduled commercial banks in government and other approved (SLR) securities. Investments in government securities include Central and State Government securities (including treasury bills) and postal obligations such as national savings certificates; 'other approved securities' are securities of state-associated bodies (electricity boards, housing boards, corporation bonds), land development bank debentures and Regional Rural Bank shares treated as approved securities under Section 5(a) of the Banking Regulation Act, 1949. RBI compiles it from the fortnightly Form A return and publishes it as item 6 'Investments' (with 6.1 Government Securities and 6.2 Other Approved Securities) in the WSS/RBI Bulletin.",
   "source_name": "RBI — A Handbook on RBI's Weekly Statistical Supplement, Section 4 (Investments)",
   "source_url": "https://rbidocs.rbi.org.in/rdocs/Publications/PDFs/HWSSF170614.pdf",
